@startuml Kiwi_Capture_Processing
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #216875
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 24
title Capture processing: score as-received and diagnostic profiles separately
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Original audio / IQ\nimmutable + hashed" as Original
rectangle "Continuity / settings\n+ eligibility checks" as Check
rectangle "Versioned demodulation\n+ resample to 48 kHz" as Import
rectangle "As-received profile\nfixed conversion scale" as Raw
rectangle "Diagnostic profile\nexplicit correction recipe" as Diagnostic
rectangle "Continuous replay\nBW500 pilot acquisition\nCRC validation" as Decode
rectangle "Stratified report\npaired results + exclusions" as Report
rectangle "Invalid capture intervals\nretain evidence + reasons" as Invalid
Original --> Check
Check --> Import : eligible intervals
Check --> Invalid : invalid intervals
Import --> Raw
Import --> Diagnostic
Raw --> Decode
Diagnostic --> Decode
Decode --> Report : separate profile labels
Invalid --> Report : separate denominator
note bottom of Import
Keep original-to-derived sample
mapping and guards. Replay the entire
continuous eligible interval.
Never interpolate a gap and call it a
valid RF observation.
GNSS/timing, SNR/amplitude and decode
eligibility are distinct.
end note
@enduml
